    "text": "They said there's a limit, and as you can't exceed, without becoming something else, I didn't know you could feel like this. I keep adding weight to who I am, every proof, every second hand plan, stacking expectations in my chest, approximations I never fully test, they talk in numbers quiet and precise, like certainty is something you can slice, but every measure I align, feels like it fractures over time, not quite stable, not quite mine, somewhere near a boundary line. I feel the curve start to redefine, and my past the point, where I can hold this form, where the pressure builds in the self-defense. If I cross that line, do I disappear or collapse into something more severe? They call it limit, like it's clean and defined, but it feels like losing my mind. Everybody says you're not enough, but dresses it in polished stuff. Equations I don't understand, still somehow written in my hands, a bright white heart, compressed and tight, holding out against the night, but every doubt I try to hide, that's another layer deep inside. I'm still standing, but I've been the fragile state of our word, calm while everything is towards the dawn, in my past the point, where I can hold this form, where the pressure builds in the self-defense. If I cross that line, do I disappear or collapse into something more severe? They call it limit, like it's just a line, but it feels like it's wallow in mine. 1.44 They said it like a threshold, like a warning sign, like if I reached it, I'd stop being fine. But what happens to everything I carried here? All the small lights compressed into fear? Does it disappear or ignite? I start to feel the edge of strain, the quiet shift beneath the name. No single soft can hold the weight of every doubt I fabricate, and maybe breaking isn't lost, but just a different kind of cost, where something dense and undefined becomes a new state over time. Not an ending, just a change in time. If I pass the point, where I can't stay the same, and the pressure burns through the fragile frame, maybe what I lose is what I outgrew, and the collapse is just breaking through, they call it limit, but it might be a door to something I wasn't before. Somewhere beyond the way I hold, there's a quiet wall I didn't know. Not failure. Transformation. Written and pressure. In constellation.",
